            },
            "dataSources": {
                "primary": "ds_CyhUhOAt"
            },
            "options": {
                "backgroundColor": "#16253D",
                "columnFormat": {
                    "description": {
                        "align": "auto",
                        "data": "> table | seriesByName(\"description\") | formatByType(descriptionColumnFormatEditorConfig)",
                        "headerAlign": "auto",
                        "rowBackgroundColors": "> table | seriesByName(\"description\") | matchValue(descriptionRowBackgroundColorsEditorConfig)",
                        "rowColors": "> table | seriesByName('description') | pick(descriptionRowColorsEditorConfig)",
                        "textOverflow": "break-word"
                    },
                    "index": {
                        "align": "auto",
                        "data": "> table | seriesByName(\"index\") | formatByType(indexColumnFormatEditorConfig)",
                        "headerAlign": "auto",
                        "rowBackgroundColors": "> table | seriesByName('index') | matchValue(indexRowBackgroundColorsEditorConfig)",
                        "rowColors": "> table | seriesByName('index') | pick(indexRowColorsEditorConfig)",
                        "textOverflow": "break-word"
                    },
                    "keywords": {
                        "align": "auto",
                        "data": "> table | seriesByName(\"keywords\") | formatByType(keywordsColumnFormatEditorConfig)",
                        "headerAlign": "auto",
                        "rowBackgroundColors": "> table | seriesByName(\"keywords\") | matchValue(keywordsRowBackgroundColorsEditorConfig)",
                        "rowColors": "> table | seriesByName('keywords') | pick(keywordsRowColorsEditorConfig)",
                        "textOverflow": "break-word"
                    },
                    "sourcetype": {
                        "align": "auto",
                        "data": "> table | seriesByName(\"sourcetype\") | formatByType(sourcetypeColumnFormatEditorConfig)",
                        "headerAlign": "auto",
                        "rowBackgroundColors": "> table | seriesByName(\"sourcetype\") | matchValue(sourcetypeRowBackgroundColorsEditorConfig)",
                        "rowColors": "> table | seriesByName('sourcetype') | pick(sourcetypeRowColorsEditorConfig)",
                        "textOverflow": "break-word"
                    }
                },
                "count": 20,
                "dataOverlayMode": "none",
                "drilldown": "none",
                "showInternalFields": false,
                "tableFormat": {
                    "headerAlign": "left",
                    "headerBackgroundColor": "> backgroundColor | setColorChannel(tableHeaderBackgroundColorConfig)",
                    "headerColor": "> headerBackgroundColor | maxContrast(tableRowColorMaxContrast)",
                    "rowBackgroundColors": "> table | seriesByIndex(0) | pick(tableAltRowBackgroundColorsByBackgroundColor)",
                    "rowColors": "> rowBackgroundColors | maxContrast(tableRowColorMaxContrast)"
                }
            },
            "showProgressBar": true,
            "title": "",
            "type": "splunk.table"
        },
        "viz_LslAH2xt": {
            "options": {
                "fontColor": "#ffffff",
                "fontSize": "large",
                "markdown": "## Template Requirements\n\nTo use this dashboard, upload a lookup containing the following fields:\n\n- index\n- sourcetype\n- description\n- keywords\n\nThe dashboard is configured to reference this lookup when displaying searchable index and sourcetype information.\n\n## Customization\n\nFeel free to modify the lookup structure to meet your organization's needs. Additional fields can be added and existing fields can be renamed as long as the dashboard searches are updated accordingly.\n\nRecommended customizations:\n\n- Update button labels and keyword categories to match your environment\n- Modify descriptions to align with your data sources\n- Add organization-specific metadata fields\n- Adjust filters and search criteria as needed\n\n## Example Lookup Structure\n\n| index | sourcetype | description | keywords |\n|---------|---------|---------|---------|\n| example_index | example_sourcetype | Description of the data source | security, authentication, endpoint |\n\n**Note:** If field names are changed, update all associated searches, filters, and button actions within the dashboard source code."
            },
            "type": "splunk.markdown"
        },
        "viz_UkMC7XPg": {
            "options": {
                "customFontSize": 25,
                "fontSize": "custom",
                "markdown": "Popular Searches"
            },
            "type": "splunk.markdown"
        },
        "viz_WVhduOFR": {
            "options": {
                "customFontSize": 20,
                "fontSize": "custom",
                "markdown": "Search by business terms or technology names to discover avaialble data. Examples: MFA, VPN, Firewall"
            },
            "type": "splunk.markdown"
        },
